# UBSan suppressions for run-fuzzers: findings already triaged, so the
# fuzzers keep looking for new ones instead of stopping on these. Remove
# an entry once the bug is fixed upstream. Format: <check>:<function|file>.
# Inlined helpers have to be matched by file: UBSan matches the function
# name of the outermost (non-inlined) frame.
#
# BIRD idiom, not a memory bug: a typed net_addr_<type> (e.g. a stack
# net_addr_ip6, 24 bytes) is passed as the generic net_addr * (40 bytes) and
# its fields read through the lib/net.h accessors. The fields read are inside
# the real object (ASan agrees); only the declared type is larger. First hit:
# babel_write_source_prefix() -> put_ip6_px() -> net_pxlen().
object-size:lib/net.h
#
# Known finding: rip_check_authentication() (cryptographic auth) places
# struct rip_auth_tail at pkt + packet_len, a value from the packet, before
# the MAC check; an odd packet_len makes the u16 reads and the memset32()
# misaligned (packets.c:385). Harmless on x86, a fault on strict-alignment
# CPUs. Covers all alignment reports in that file (UBSan cannot match the
# inlined function). Remove once fixed.
alignment:proto/rip/packets.c
